+
+This skill gracefully STOPS the running mj-agent local-dev app runtime — non-destructive, all data preserved — as the reversible counterpart to mj-agent-infra-app-start. Its net-new capability is stopping host-run processes (LangGraph Studio on :2024 / Chainlit on its configured port) via port-owner tree-kill (taskkill /T /F, since `mj-agent serve` spawns a chainlit child); it also runs Level-1 `docker compose … down` (keeps volumes + images) for the container stack, verifies everything stopped, and hands destructive cleanup off to mj-agent-infra-env-teardown. Note graceful stop is best-effort on Windows (force-kill; container-down timeout requires target reconciliation and Owner decision, never an automatic kill fallback). Make sure to use this skill whenever the user says "停掉 mj-agent", "关掉 app", "stop the app", "stop mj-agent", "关闭本地开发环境", "把 Studio 停了", "停掉 serve", "shut down the agent". Do not use for: destructive docker cleanup / volume wipe / local image removal (use mj-agent-infra-env-teardown Level 2/3); the low-level compose down primitive (use mj-agent-infra-docker-compose); starting the app (use mj-agent-infra-app-start); pg_dump backup before a wipe (use mj-agent-infra-storage-stack).
